WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.545
The observed moment comes from one finite
data sample.

2
00:00:03.545 --> 00:00:08.160
Its sampling error remains fixed while we
compare the model with that target.

3
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:17.895
At one candidate parameter, simulated data
approximate the model's expected moment.

4
00:00:17.895 --> 00:00:22.936
With only a few simulations, that
approximation contains simulation error.

5
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.480
Average more simulated data sets.

6
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.610
Simulation error shrinks on average,

7
00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:32.871
although one particular sequence need not
improve at every step.

8
00:00:32.871 --> 00:00:35.001
The observed target stays put.

9
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:42.143
In this lesson, SMM approaches the direct
GMM estimate for the same data sample.

10
00:00:42.143 --> 00:00:44.626
More simulation improves the model
prediction;

11
00:00:44.626 --> 00:00:47.522
it does not create more observed data.
